Assignment 1.1.2 + 1.1.3
----------------------------------------
1. Open 2 ubuntu + 1 powershell terminals, in the powershell run
    python .\cam2image_host2vm\videoserver.python

    In the first ubuntu terminal, run
    ros2 run ros2 run cam2image_vm2ros cam2image--ros-args --params-file src/cam2image_vm2ros/config/cam2image.yaml

    In the second ubuntu terminal, run
    ros2 run brightness_pkg brightness

    Then open another ubuntu terminal and run e.g.
    ros2 param set brightness brightness_threshold 100

Assignment 1.1.4
----------------------------------------
1. Open 2 ubuntu + 1 powershell terminals, in the powershell run
    python .\cam2image_host2vm\videoserver.python

    In the first ubuntu terminal, run
    ros2 run ros2 run cam2image_vm2ros cam2image--ros-args --params-file src/cam2image_vm2ros/config/cam2image.yaml

    In the second ubuntu terminal, run
    ros2 run object_detection_pkg object_detection_node

Assignment 1.2.1
----------------------------------------
1. Open sequence_generator_pkg/src/sequence_generator_node.cpp
    In the parse_parameters() function, change assignment_selecter to false

    Open 1 ubuntu + 1 powershell terminals, in the powershell run
    python .\cam2image_host2vm\videoserver.python

    In the ubuntu terminal, run 
    ros2 run sequence_generator_pkg sequence_generator_launch.xml

Assignment 1.2.2
----------------------------------------
1. Open sequence_generator_pkg/src/sequence_generator_node.cpp
    In the parse_parameters() function, change assignment_selecter to true

    Open 1 ubuntu + 1 powershell terminals, in the powershell run
    python .\cam2image_host2vm\videoserver.python

    In the ubuntu terminal, run 
    ros2 run sequence_generator_pkg sequence_generator_launch.xml